<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::capital_flow_to_ai_compu" target="france_bond_crisis::auction_primary_demand" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Large new allocations into AI-compute funds and megafunds divert institutional cash that would otherwise participate in sovereign bond auctions, reducing subscription and cover ratios at French primary auctions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">france_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::capital_flow_to_ai_compu" target="france_bond_crisis::cross_border_capflow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge of foreign capital chasing AI compute investments (largely domiciled in US/Asia) produces net outflows from French bond and equity markets as investors rebalance into higher-return tech allocations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">france_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_trade::capital_flow_to_ai_compu" target="germany_industry_transit::supply_chain_vuln" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A reallocation of new AI‑compute capital toward US/China actors secures long‑term offtake and capacity through investment and contracts outside Europe, reducing available commercial capacity for German firms and increasing their exposure to concentrated external suppliers.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_trade</data>
  <data key="d39">germany_industry_transit</data>
</edge>
